# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Session Workflow

Full guidelines (architecture, anti-patterns, visual system) are in `AGENTS.md` — read it at the start of every session.

## Mandatory 5-Step Flow

### 1. DISCOVER — before writing any code in `src/app/`

Read these indices first:
- `indices/COMPONENTS.md` — existing UI components
- `indices/SERVICES.md` + `indices/FACADES.md` — existing services and facades
- `indices/MODELS.md` — existing TypeScript interfaces
- `indices/DIRECTIVES.md`, `indices/PIPES.md`, `indices/STORES.md`
- `indices/DATABASE.md` — Supabase tables (if applicable)
- `context/domain.md` + `context/brief.md` — business context and today's objective

**Never create something that already exists. Reuse first, create second.**

### 2. PLAN — state scope before coding

List every file you will touch. If the task spans more than 2 files, write out your plan explicitly before starting.

### 3. EXECUTE — follow all rules in AGENTS.md

One vertical slice at a time: the smallest usable piece, across the layers it needs — never all the database first, then the UI. Commit the failing test alone before the code that makes it pass. Reuse existing components, facades, and models. New components go in the canonical folder structure (`core/`, `features/`, `shared/`, `layout/`).

### 4. VALIDATE

Run `npm run lint:arch` after making changes to verify architectural compliance.

### 5. SYNC — update indices at end of session

Update `indices/*.md` with any new components, services, facades, models, or database changes you created.
